===Etymology===
From {{der|en|grc|-}} {{af|grc|σπέρμα|t1=sperm|ζῷον|t2=living thing|nocat=1}}, equivalent to {{af|en|spermato-|-zoon}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˌspɜːmətə(ʊ)ˈzəʊɒn/|a=UK}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-spermatozoon.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|spermatozoa}}

# {{lb|en|cytology}} A reproductive cell or [[gamete]] of a male, carried in [[semen]], that fertilizes an [[ovum]] to produce a [[zygote]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2019|author=w:Bill Bryson|title=The Body: A Guide for Occupants|publisher=Black Swan (2020)|page=339|passage=But let us suppose [...] that one hardy or lucky '''spermatozoon''' has reached the waiting egg.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Dr. Steve Chapman|title=Is swallowing semen good for you?|magazine=Better2Know|url=https://www.better2know.co.uk/blog/is-swallowing-semen-good-for-you/|date=2024-06-11|passage=A sperm, or '''spermatozoa''', is the microscopic male reproductive cell. Sperms are made up of oval-shaped heads and long tails that they use for mobility.}}

